WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.099
Office Party and Team Events.

2
00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:06.305
Day 78 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:09.079
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.359 --> 00:00:12.004
An office party is still work, just more relaxed.

5
00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:15.932
People remember how you made them feel, not what you said about Kafka.

6
00:00:16.212 --> 00:00:19.519
Turn up, mix with people, be warm, and leave on a good note.

7
00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:21.722
Part 1.

8
00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:23.303
The party game plan.

9
00:00:24.553 --> 00:00:25.471
Step 1:

10
00:00:25.751 --> 00:00:29.271
Arrive: within the first 30 minutes, when groups are still forming.

11
00:00:29.551 --> 00:00:30.468
Step 2:

12
00:00:30.748 --> 00:00:33.500
Greet: your manager or host first, then your team.

13
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.697
Step 3:

14
00:00:34.977 --> 00:00:38.071
Mix: talk to 3 people outside your usual circle.

15
00:00:38.351 --> 00:00:39.311
Step 4:

16
00:00:39.591 --> 00:00:43.665
Enjoy: join the games, food, photos; don't hide behind your phone.

17
00:00:43.945 --> 00:00:44.905
Step 5:

18
00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:48.471
Exit: thank the organisers and leave while you're still fresh.

19
00:00:49.821 --> 00:00:50.695
Part 2.

20
00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:52.618
Openers that always work.

21
00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.447
With colleagues you barely know.

22
00:00:55.727 --> 00:00:57.945
Hi, I'm Ashish from the checkout team.

23
00:00:58.225 --> 00:00:59.911
I don't think we've properly met!

24
00:01:00.191 --> 00:01:01.983
How long have you been with the company?

25
00:01:02.263 --> 00:01:03.500
Which team are you on?

26
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.423
What are you working on these days?

27
00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:08.010
With senior leaders.

28
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.706
Hi Ma'am or Sir, I'm Ashish, I work on the delivery-tracking feature.

29
00:01:12.986 --> 00:01:15.162
Great event, thanks for organising it.

30
00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.362
What's been the highlight of the year for you?

31
00:01:17.642 --> 00:01:20.287
Is there anything you're excited about for next year?

32
00:01:21.637 --> 00:01:22.277
Tip.

33
00:01:22.557 --> 00:01:24.413
Keep it short (2 to 3 minutes).

34
00:01:24.693 --> 00:01:26.613
Leaders want to meet many people.

35
00:01:26.893 --> 00:01:30.072
Don't pitch projects or ask for a promotion at a party.

36
00:01:31.422 --> 00:01:32.787
About the event itself.

37
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.198
The food's great.

38
00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:36.078
Have you tried the biryani?

39
00:01:36.358 --> 00:01:37.723
Are you joining the quiz?

40
00:01:38.003 --> 00:01:39.646
We need one more for our team.

41
00:01:39.926 --> 00:01:41.227
Who organised this?

42
00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:42.809
They did a great job.

43
00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:45.737
Personal (safe) topics.

44
00:01:46.017 --> 00:01:47.596
Any plans for the holidays?

45
00:01:47.876 --> 00:01:49.732
Have you watched anything good lately?

46
00:01:50.012 --> 00:01:51.548
Where are you from originally?

47
00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:53.769
Do you do anything fun on weekends?

48
00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:55.201
Sports, music?

49
00:01:56.551 --> 00:01:57.447
Part 3.

50
00:01:57.727 --> 00:01:59.349
Joining and leaving groups.

51
00:02:00.599 --> 00:02:01.943
Here is a quick table:

52
00:02:02.223 --> 00:02:04.079
Situation, and Say or do.

53
00:02:04.359 --> 00:02:05.319
Join a group:

54
00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:08.137
Stand at the edge, smile, wait for a pause:

55
00:02:08.417 --> 00:02:09.761
Mind if I join you?

56
00:02:10.041 --> 00:02:11.151
Bring someone in:

57
00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.031
Priya, have you met Arjun?

58
00:02:13.311 --> 00:02:15.124
He's the one who built the new search.

59
00:02:15.404 --> 00:02:16.748
Leave a conversation:

60
00:02:17.028 --> 00:02:18.073
Great chatting!

61
00:02:18.353 --> 00:02:19.911
I'm going to grab some food.

62
00:02:20.191 --> 00:02:21.215
Catch you later.

63
00:02:21.495 --> 00:02:22.583
Leave the party:

64
00:02:22.863 --> 00:02:25.764
Thanks so much for organising, I had a great time.

65
00:02:26.044 --> 00:02:27.068
See you Monday!

66
00:02:28.418 --> 00:02:29.335
Part 4.

67
00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.429
Toasts, speeches and awards.

68
00:02:32.679 --> 00:02:33.959
Giving a short toast.

69
00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:35.177
You could say:

70
00:02:35.457 --> 00:02:37.889
Can I have everyone's attention for one minute?

71
00:02:38.169 --> 00:02:44.932
This year we launched 3 cities and survived two sale days without downtime, and that's because of everyone in this room.

72
00:02:45.212 --> 00:02:48.007
Special thanks to the platform team for the late nights.

73
00:02:48.287 --> 00:02:49.801
To an even better next year.

74
00:02:50.081 --> 00:02:50.892
Cheers!

75
00:02:52.242 --> 00:02:57.447
Under 60 seconds, one specific achievement, thank people by name, end with a cheer.

76
00:02:58.797 --> 00:03:00.056
Receiving an award.

77
00:03:00.336 --> 00:03:01.275
You could say:

78
00:03:01.555 --> 00:03:03.560
Thank you, I'm honestly surprised!

79
00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.205
This was a team effort.

80
00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:09.091
Meena, Ravi and Kavya did the heavy lifting on the migration.

81
00:03:09.371 --> 00:03:10.331
Thank you all.

82
00:03:11.681 --> 00:03:13.665
Asked to say something unexpectedly.

83
00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:14.883
You could say:

84
00:03:15.163 --> 00:03:16.550
I wasn't expecting this!

85
00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:17.769
I'll just say:

86
00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:21.462
I've learned more this year than in the last three, thanks to this team.

87
00:03:21.742 --> 00:03:22.595
Thank you!

88
00:03:23.945 --> 00:03:24.905
Part 5.

89
00:03:25.185 --> 00:03:26.807
Etiquette: do's and don'ts.

90
00:03:28.057 --> 00:03:29.401
Here is a quick table:

91
00:03:29.681 --> 00:03:30.683
Do, and Don't.

92
00:03:30.963 --> 00:03:33.182
Dress one step smarter than the dress code:

93
00:03:33.462 --> 00:03:36.491
Drink too much; know your limit (or stick to mocktails).

94
00:03:36.771 --> 00:03:37.945
Put your phone away:

95
00:03:38.225 --> 00:03:41.105
Talk about work problems, salaries or appraisals.

96
00:03:41.385 --> 00:03:43.603
Talk to new joiners and quiet people:

97
00:03:43.883 --> 00:03:46.699
Gossip or complain about colleagues or managers.

98
00:03:46.979 --> 00:03:49.518
Take part in games, even if you're bad at them:

99
00:03:49.798 --> 00:03:52.059
Stay only with your own team all evening.

100
00:03:52.339 --> 00:03:53.747
Thank the organisers:

101
00:03:54.027 --> 00:03:56.865
Make jokes about religion, politics, appearance.

102
00:03:57.145 --> 00:03:59.833
Respect people who don't drink or eat certain food:

103
00:04:00.113 --> 00:04:02.651
Pressure anyone to drink, dance or loosen up.

104
00:04:04.001 --> 00:04:04.748
Warning:

105
00:04:05.028 --> 00:04:06.351
The next-morning test.

106
00:04:06.631 --> 00:04:08.657
Before you say or post something, ask:

107
00:04:08.937 --> 00:04:12.820
Would I be comfortable if my manager and HR heard this on Monday?

108
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.425
Party photos and videos travel fast.

109
00:04:16.775 --> 00:04:17.714
Part 6.

110
00:04:17.994 --> 00:04:19.039
For introverts.

111
00:04:20.289 --> 00:04:21.207
Set a goal:

112
00:04:21.487 --> 00:04:24.772
3 meaningful conversations, then you're allowed to leave.

113
00:04:25.052 --> 00:04:26.865
Volunteer to help organise.

114
00:04:27.145 --> 00:04:29.833
It gives you a role and natural reasons to talk.

115
00:04:30.113 --> 00:04:31.159
Arrive early.

116
00:04:31.439 --> 00:04:33.657
Small groups are easier than a full room.

117
00:04:33.937 --> 00:04:35.644
Stand near the food or drinks.

118
00:04:35.924 --> 00:04:37.097
People come to you.

119
00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.511
Ask questions and let others talk.

120
00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:41.839
Good listeners are always welcome.

121
00:04:43.189 --> 00:04:44.127
Part 7.

122
00:04:44.407 --> 00:04:46.050
For seniors and managers.

123
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.247
Go round every table, especially to people who don't normally see you.

124
00:04:51.527 --> 00:04:53.873
Thank people publicly for specific work.

125
00:04:54.153 --> 00:04:56.009
Make sure new joiners are included.

126
00:04:56.289 --> 00:05:00.748
Leave a little early so the team can relax, and settle any team bill quietly.

127
00:05:02.098 --> 00:05:02.973
Part 8.

128
00:05:03.253 --> 00:05:04.639
Practice conversation:

129
00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:06.754
Meeting a senior leader at a party.

130
00:05:08.004 --> 00:05:10.031
Here is how the conversation goes.

131
00:05:10.311 --> 00:05:12.913
Hi, I'm Ashish from the checkout team.

132
00:05:13.193 --> 00:05:15.817
Great event, thanks for organising it.

133
00:05:16.097 --> 00:05:17.143
Hi Ashish!

134
00:05:17.423 --> 00:05:18.916
Glad you're enjoying it.

135
00:05:19.196 --> 00:05:20.391
What do you work on?

136
00:05:20.671 --> 00:05:22.356
The delivery-slot feature.

137
00:05:22.636 --> 00:05:25.303
We launched it in three new cities this year.

138
00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:26.969
Oh, that was your team?

139
00:05:27.249 --> 00:05:28.615
That was a big win.

140
00:05:29.965 --> 00:05:31.565
The conversation continues.

141
00:05:31.845 --> 00:05:32.783
Thank you.

142
00:05:33.063 --> 00:05:34.919
It was a real team effort.

143
00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:37.653
What's been the highlight of the year for you?

144
00:05:37.933 --> 00:05:39.661
Honestly, seeing the team grow.

145
00:05:39.941 --> 00:05:41.733
We hired forty people this year.

146
00:05:42.013 --> 00:05:43.186
That's amazing.

147
00:05:43.466 --> 00:05:45.002
Well, I won't keep you.

148
00:05:45.282 --> 00:05:46.626
Enjoy the evening!

149
00:05:46.906 --> 00:05:47.973
You too.

150
00:05:48.253 --> 00:05:49.810
Nice meeting you, Ashish.

151
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.696
That's the end of this lesson.

152
00:05:52.976 --> 00:05:57.627
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

153
00:05:57.907 --> 00:06:04.029
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

